  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Penang popular theatre-song form rooted in nineteenth-century Muharram street performance, now staged as a comic sketch followed by songs. A tukang karang (lead singer and lyricist) sings topical verses answered by a dancing chorus, accompanied by violins, gambus lute (the oud card stands in), tabla and marwas hand drums (the membrane-drum card stands in), often with accordion, cymbals and harmonica as well.",
